B.b5g=new A.bQ("This project is community-driven and not affiliated with the original shadcn/ui project.",null)
B.b5h=new A.bQ("Themes are registry-owned presets. The CLI lists available presets and applies generated theme artifacts to your project. Assets are installed through registry bootstrap actions so fonts and icon files are copied to the right location and recorded in project state.",null)
B.b5i=new A.bQ("For machine-readable automation, use --json on read-only commands such as registries, list, search, info, dry-run, validate, audit, deps, and doctor.",null)
B.b5j=new A.bQ("Text styling is provided through extensions on Widget. Use chained modifiers to create headings, captions, and inline emphasis without custom TextStyle boilerplate.",null)
B.b5k=new A.bQ("Production-ready error handling that maps exceptions into a single AppError model and renders consistent UI across your app. It provides dual-scope error channels for app-level and screen-level errors.",null)
B.b5l=new A.bQ("Install via the CLI:",null)
B.b5m=new A.bQ("Here you can find all the components available in the library. We are working on adding more components.",null)
B.b5n=new A.bQ("Use ShadcnApp if you want a convenience wrapper that applies theme defaults and ShadcnLayer for you.",null)
B.b5o=new A.bQ("Theme via ComponentTheme<ErrorSystemTheme>:",null)
B.b5p=new A.bQ("Shared helpers are declared once under shared[] in components.json and referenced by each component entry. This keeps installs lean and avoids duplicating primitives.",null)
B.b5q=new A.bQ("ShadcnApp keeps the compatibility bootstrap path by default: it preloads all generated component theme globals once. If you want a narrower startup surface, import component_theme_global_configs.dart, call only the registrars for the installed components you use, and set preloadComponentThemeGlobals to false on ShadcnApp.",null)
B.b5r=new A.bQ("This guide covers the full flutter_shadcn workflow from installation through production QA. The CLI copies registry-owned Flutter components into your app, records what it installed under .shadcn, and keeps dependency, theme, asset, and diagnostic workflows in one place.",null)
B.b5t=new A.bQ("The main Dart file should match the component ID, and any helper classes go under _impl/. Use README.md for human docs and preview.dart for gallery previews.",null)
B.b5u=new A.bQ("Only use this if you are not using ShadcnLayer. It provides the overlay manager without other defaults.",null)
B.b5v=new A.bQ("Every component should include a meta.json file describing its ID, name, category, and dependencies. The CLI uses this to build the catalog and to resolve shared helpers.",null)
B.b5w=new A.bQ("Use namespace-qualified component addresses when you have more than one registry enabled or want to be explicit.",null)
B.b5x=new A.bQ("Install all components from the active registry:",null)
B.b5y=new A.bQ("shadcn_flutter components are state-management agnostic. You can use setState, ValueNotifier, Provider, Riverpod, Bloc, or any architecture that fits your app.",null)
B.b5z=new A.bQ("This toolkit is actively evolving. Expect occasional API changes while the registry and docs stabilize.",null)
B.b5A=new A.bQ("Add the pub cache bin directory to your PATH if needed. The CLI also provides a short alias: `shadcn`.",null)
B.b5B=new A.bQ("Global flags: --verbose prints extra detail, --offline disables network calls, --registry-name selects a namespace, and --advanced enables developer registry overrides plus experimental tooling.",null)
B.b5C=new A.bQ("Use local registry mode for development, or remote/CDN mode for production installs. You can also persist dev mode globally for your workspace.",null)
B.b5D=new A.bQ("Import the icon constants and render them with the Icon widget. Combine with text for buttons and labels.",null)
B.b5E=new A.bQ("Initialize the registry install path and shared assets. The docs app uses `lib/ui/shadcn`.",null)
B.b5F=new A.bQ("Add custom rules to map your domain-specific errors. Rules are evaluated in order, so place more specific matches first.",null)
B.b5G=new A.bQ("Add multiple components at once:",null)
B.b5H=new A.bQ("1) Create an ErrorMapper (once)",null)
B.b5I=new A.bQ("Useful links: grab the CLI, browse the GitHub repo, and inspect the registry source.",null)
B.b5J=new A.bQ("Remove a component:",null)
B.b5K=new A.bQ("2) Base repository",null)
B.b5L=new A.bQ("Control optional files during install:",null)
B.b5M=new A.bQ("If your registry lives under flutter_shadcn_kit/lib/registry, the manifest source paths should start with that prefix (for example flutter_shadcn_kit/lib/registry/components/...).",null)
B.b5N=new A.bQ("Pick registry presets, mix base and accent from different themes, and preview the result in a full component kitchen.",null)
B.b5O=new A.bQ("A registry is just a folder tree plus a manifest file that describes every component, its dependencies, and the files to copy. The CLI reads the manifest, copies files into the consumer project, and wires dependencies and assets.",null)
B.b5P=new A.bQ("Local registry development is advanced mode. Use it only when authoring or testing a registry before publishing.",null)
B.b5Q=new A.bQ("3) Use in repositories",null)
B.b5R=new A.bQ("components.json is the source of truth. It declares defaults, shared file mappings, and every component entry. The CLI validates it against components.schema.json.",null)
B.b5S=new A.bQ("Recommended root wrapper. It injects overlay handling for popovers, tooltips, menus, and drawers.",null)
B.b5T=new A.bQ("Use ShadcnLayer at the app root to enable overlays and theme primitives. OverlayManagerLayer is only needed if you are not using ShadcnLayer. ShadcnApp is a convenience wrapper that sets up theme + ShadcnLayer for you.",null)
B.b5U=new A.bQ("Use guard() for small call sites without a ScreenErrorScope.",null)
B.b5V=new A.bQ("For local development, pass a registry path on disk so the CLI can copy files directly.",null)
B.b5W=new A.bQ("Semantic colors are exposed through Theme.of(context).colorScheme. These drive component defaults and keep surfaces, borders, and accents consistent.",null)
B.b5X=new A.bQ("For production checks, run the CLI diagnostics and Flutter verification commands in the same app where components are installed.",null)
